statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ and write Hᵏ = μHE[k]. Assume:
- ψ : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P is C¹, V ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} is open, ψ is injective on V and Dψ(y) is injective for y ∈ V;
- F : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ is C¹;
- Y' ⊆ V is Borel with DF(y) ≠ 0 for all y ∈ Y';
- G : ℝ^P → ℝ^P satisfies G(ψ(y)) ∈ Dψ(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) and ⟨G(ψ(y)), Dψ(y)e⟩ = DF(y)e for y ∈ Y' and e ∈ ℝ^{n+1}.
Then for every Borel g : ℝ^P → [0,∞], the function t ↦ ∫_{ψ(Y'∩F⁻¹(t))} g dHⁿ is Borel and ∫_ℝ ∫_{ψ(Y'∩F⁻¹(t))} g dHⁿ dt = ∫_{ψ(Y')} |G| g dH^{n+1}.
